  {:path "lang/compat/clojure/string.kotoba"
   :kind :shim
   :forwards-to kotoba.string
   :provides #{starts-with? ends-with? includes?
               blank? trim triml trimr reverse
               index-of last-index-of}
   :equivalence :exact
   :shim
   {:as-of "2026-09-08"
    :why-not-deleted "74 guest .kotoba modules require it, measured rather than assumed: `grep -rl --include='*.kotoba' '\\[clojure\\.string' orgs | wc -l` -> 74, of which network-awai/app-hyakka 66, kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics 6, kotoba-lang/lang-pure-wt 1, kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang 1. Deleting the namespace stops all 74 resolving their (:require [clojure.string :as str]). Rewriting those call sites is a separate migration with its own decision; a rename does not travel on the back of an unrelated change."
    :removal-condition "this file goes when that count reaches 0. Re-running the one command above is the whole of the check; nothing else has to be decided."
    :shape "forwarding wrappers, because a bare re-export is NOT expressible here. Measured 2026-09-08 at amu 9092ee34: (ns kotoba.text (:require [kotoba.string :as ks]) (:export [byte-index-of])) with no definition is refused :kotoba.error/export-names-undefined, \"namespace exports must name declared public functions: byte-index-of is not defined in this module\". So each name is a one-line call into kotoba.string -- one implementation, one extra call frame."
    :drift-guard "a forwarder that reimplemented its body, or forwarded to a different name, would compile and would pass every behaviour test, because those run the canonical module. test/kotoba/lang/clojure_string_compat_test.cljk reads the forwarders and asserts each is a single call to the SAME name in kotoba.string."
    :does-not-carry-join "join is in kotoba.string.join, not here. Putting it here would make all 74 call sites above need an amu that lowers typed-list-nth, which is the defect this arrangement exists to avoid -- measured, see :modules :kotoba.string.join :measured."}
   :absent
